<article class="env-lemma" id="0325">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0325">Lemma <span data-tag="0325">10.160.2</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian complete local ring. Any quotient of $R$ is also a Noetherian complete local ring. Given a finite ring map $R \to S$, then $S$ is a product of Noetherian complete local rings. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The ring $S$ is Noetherian by Lemma <a href="/tag/00FN" data-tag="00FN">10.31.1</a>. As an $R$-module $S$ is complete by Lemma <a href="/tag/00MA" data-tag="00MA">10.97.1</a>. Hence $S$ is the product of the completions at its maximal ideals by Lemma <a href="/tag/07N9" data-tag="07N9">10.97.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>